\subsection*{Entity Analysis}

The program performs a textual analysis of a document by identifying entities and locating them within the text. It begins by reading the text file using the \texttt{read\_document} function and cleaning it with the \texttt{trim\_text\_edges} function.

Named entities, such as people, organizations, and locations, are automatically extracted using the \texttt{find\_entities} function, which leverages spaCy's NLP model (vide \textit{Resources}). For each entity, the program returns its category and all positions where it occurs in the text.

In addition to automatic entity recognition, the program allows for manual searches to find positions of unrecognized entities using the \texttt{find\_words} function.

These two results are then combined, producing a structured mapping of both automatically and manually found entities to their positions in the text. Along with the total word count (important for reference, as positions are relative), the results are printed and saved in JSON format using the \texttt{save\_json} function, enabling further analysis or visualization.

Finally, the results are visualized using the \texttt{plot\_entities\_positions\_from\_json} function, allowing the selection of categories to visualize and the exclusion of specific entities. This flexibility ensures the visualization highlights the most relevant data.

